    "updated_at": "2025-07-23T09:06:00Z",
    "body": "Hi, I had tested with the dev branch previously, but just confirmed the same behavior with v1.30.0 from the registry:\n```\n$ podman run  \\\n  --rm --name homarr \\\n  -p 7575:7575 \\\n  -e SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY='1ce680cf744e7b0da0d8a175b3207ecd382578cd2cce611f31f6f4a701fda645' \\\n  -d ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr:v1.30.0\n5c8a70707f45cf3ce67f76fbe5959d63a9fd4730c5d3bf13124966406e8245be\n\n$ podman stop homarr\nWARN[0010] StopSignal SIGTERM failed to stop container homarr in 10 seconds, resorting to SIGKILL \nhomarr\n```\n\nInspecting container logs with `podman logs -f homarr` seem to indicate the same behavior (receiving SIGTERM, logging it, then continuing to run):\n```\nReceived SIGTERM. Shutting down...\n2025-07-23T08:35:32.489Z info: SIGTERM\n2025-07-23T08:35:32.575Z info: \u2796 Connection (0) 1006\n```\n\n**Edit:** Additionally, it seems that even after setting the `DISABLE_REDIS_LOGS` envvar, the container will fail to stop. It seems that bash `wait` without any arguments will wait for _all_ background tasks to finish. I had forgot to mention previously that locally I changed\nhttps://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/blob/d218170ec28a70b80c521efd1482164087d46e05/scripts/run.sh#L51\nto\n```bash\nwait $NGINX_PID $TASKS_PID $WSS_PID $NEXTJS_PID\n```\nsince at that point the Redis background task is not called to be terminated yet.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
