    "updated_at": "2025-08-04T06:12:20Z",
    "body": "I see the same something similar in docker:\n\nMilliseconds after running `docker compose stop homarr` I get:\n```\n21:M 04 Aug 2025 06:10:16.159 * Background saving terminated with success\nReceived SIGTERM. Shutting down...\n2025-08-04T06:10:41.056Z info: SIGTERM\n2025-08-04T06:10:41.074Z info: \u2796 Connection (2) 1006\n2025-08-04T06:10:41.099Z info: \u2796 Connection (1) 1006\n2025-08-04T06:10:41.104Z info: \u2796 Connection (0) 1006\n```\nBut after that it hangs for about 10 seconds (the default timeout) until docker's stop function times out and docker sends a SIGKILL to take down the container.",
